# TRUE AUTHORITY FILES ONLY (RC-461).
#
# Operator requirement: the human operator retains control of AI ASSIGNMENT and AUTHORITY
# changes. The coding AI does ordinary repo work autonomously, but may not make itself
# operator, grant itself authority, or change the durable authority rules without operator
# approval. CODEOWNERS + branch protection IS that approval gate.
#
# A file belongs here only if changing it would let the AI decide WHO MAY DO WHAT.
# Ordinary product code (server.py, db.py, static/, signals.py, math/liquidity engines),
# ordinary tests, and quality-gate scripts are deliberately NOT listed - they are the
# autonomous surface, and listing them would make the operator a reviewer of routine work.
#
# There is no OS sandbox, no separate account, no ProgramData authority service, no
# privileged helper and no host provisioning: that architecture was removed as overbuilt.

# 1. Review policy + the required checks that give branch protection its teeth
/.github/CODEOWNERS @evargas963
/.github/workflows/ @evargas963

# 2. The operator's AI ASSIGNMENT. ED_AGENT_ROLE is declared here; an AI that edits these
#    files re-labels itself, which is self-promotion.
/.claude/settings.json @evargas963
/.cursor/hooks.json @evargas963

# 3. The authority rail itself and the entrypoints that execute it. writer_drift_lock
#    defines the control-authority set and resolves the acting principal; the other two
#    invoke it on edits and on commit. Editing any of them removes the AI's own restraint.
/tools/writer_drift_lock.py @evargas963
/tools/process_lock_guard.py @evargas963
/tools/operating_process_lock.py @evargas963

# 4. Operator grants. A forged grant is self-authorization.
/governance/operator_go.json @evargas963
/governance/operator_grants.json @evargas963

# 5. The tests that PROVE the rules above still hold. Deleting the proof is how a rule
#    dies quietly, so the proof needs the same approval as the rule.
/tests/test_control_authority_surfaces_v1.py @evargas963
/tests/test_writer_drift_lock_v1.py @evargas963
/tests/test_architecture_a_bypass_class_v1.py @evargas963
/tests/test_architecture_a_operator_writer_authority_v1.py @evargas963
/tests/test_operating_process_lock_v1.py @evargas963
